    "titulo": "52% say inflation will ruin the holidays. Check last year's bill.",
    "descripcion": "A WalletHub survey reported on Nov 6, 2026 found about 52% of Americans think inflation will ruin their holiday season. The same survey found one in four are still paying off debt from last holiday season, and 79% have a holiday budget the same size as last year or smaller. Holiday debt mostly sits on credit cards (62% of holiday debtors in LendingTree's 2025 survey): the Federal Reserve's G.19 release puts the average rate on card accounts assessed interest at 22.36% APR in Q3 2026 (all accounts: 21.19%). Inflation raises a price once; interest on a balance you carry keeps adding to it every month. WalletHub's online survey (published Oct 7, 2026) had just over 220 respondents, weighted to U.S. demographics, so treat the percentages as rough. Survey answers are opinions, not spending data, and your own card rate may differ. Not financial advice. Sources: WalletHub via InvestigateTV, Nov 6, 2026; LendingTree via HomePage News, Jan 5, 2026; Federal Reserve G.19 Consumer Credit, Sept 2026 release.",
